WEBVTT

00:01:11.235 --> 00:01:12.615
I got a year to live, sam.

00:01:12.625 --> 00:01:13.845
I'd like to make the most of it.

00:01:13.855 --> 00:01:17.265
So what do you say we kill some evil sons
of bitches and we raise a little hell?

00:01:18.585 --> 00:01:20.215
THEN

00:01:20.225 --> 00:01:21.715
You didn't tell dean? Tell me what?

00:01:21.725 --> 00:01:23.045
There's a big new up-and-comer.

00:01:23.055 --> 00:01:23.915
Her name is lilith.

00:01:23.925 --> 00:01:27.235
She really, really wants sam's
intestines on a stick.

00:01:27.245 --> 00:01:29.075
Let dean out of his deal right now.

00:01:29.085 --> 00:01:30.225
I'm just a saleswoman.

00:01:30.235 --> 00:01:31.685
I got a boss like everybody.

00:01:31.695 --> 00:01:32.935
Who holds the contract?

00:01:32.945 --> 00:01:34.375
I can't tell you.

00:01:36.105 --> 00:01:37.865
Bela talbot's her real name.

00:01:37.905 --> 00:01:38.865
The colt.

00:01:38.885 --> 00:01:40.255
Bela stole the colt.

00:01:40.265 --> 00:01:41.325
I want it back, bela.

00:01:41.335 --> 00:01:42.805
Your little pistol, you mean?

00:01:42.915 --> 00:01:43.515
Sorry.

00:01:43.525 --> 00:01:45.965
You understand how many people
are gonna die if you do this?

00:01:45.975 --> 00:01:48.285
What exactly is it that you think
I plan to do with it?

00:01:48.295 --> 00:01:52.415
Take the only weapon we have against an army
of demons and sell it to the highest bidder.

00:01:52.565 --> 00:01:53.815
You know nothing about me.

00:01:53.845 --> 00:01:54.985
- Pack your crap.
- Why?

00:01:55.006 --> 00:01:55.995
Where are we going?

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:57.205
We're gonna go hunt the bitch down.

00:01:57.225 --> 00:01:58.235
I don't want to go to hell.

00:01:58.256 --> 00:01:59.385
We'll find a way to save you.

00:01:59.405 --> 00:02:00.715
I'm scared, sam.

00:02:00.725 --> 00:02:01.985
I'm really scared.

00:02:02.006 --> 00:02:04.825
And the only person that can get
me out of this thing is me.

00:02:04.875 --> 00:02:06.425
And me.

00:02:06.765 --> 00:02:09.275
NOW

00:02:15.235 --> 00:02:16.240
Up for a drink?

00:02:16.276 --> 00:02:18.681
No, I can't.
I got to be up at the cracky down.

00:02:18.716 --> 00:02:19.843
Duty calls.

00:02:20.235 --> 00:02:22.305
- Boob job?
- I wish.

00:02:22.339 --> 00:02:24.984
Nah, some crabby old broad
wants the works.

00:02:25.036 --> 00:02:26.808
I need a forklift to get it all back up.

00:02:26.835 --> 00:02:29.735
All that work to have what?
15 minutes off her faces?

00:02:29.770 --> 00:02:31.591
Staying young is a brutal business.

00:03:09.036 --> 00:03:09.830
Hey!

00:03:11.144 --> 00:03:12.175
Help!

00:03:16.738 --> 00:03:18.189
Let me out of here!

00:03:18.882 --> 00:03:20.498
Help!

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:34.140
- Sir?
- Please.

00:03:35.144 --> 00:03:37.367
It's okay, sir.
Let me see what happened.

00:03:39.283 --> 00:03:41.706
Don't you worry.
There's nothing I haven't seen.

00:03:42.243 --> 00:03:44.526
- No, no, no...
- Let me see...

00:03:52.435 --> 00:03:55.536
Transcript : www.1000fr.com
Synchro : Flolo

00:04:01.742 --> 00:04:02.796
Stop!

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:04.637
You ready to talk?

00:04:06.911 --> 00:04:08.105
I don't know.

00:04:08.443 --> 00:04:10.138
I don't know anything!

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:12.218
Oh, you hear that, Sam?
He doesn't know anything.

00:04:12.242 --> 00:04:13.518
Yeah, I heard.

00:04:13.542 --> 00:04:14.846
I'm telling you the truth.

00:04:14.881 --> 00:04:15.936
Oh, you are?

00:04:16.042 --> 00:04:18.216
My god,
then I owe you an apology.

00:04:18.242 --> 00:04:19.906
Allow me to make it up to you.

00:04:28.043 --> 00:04:30.137
I'm gonna ask you one last time...

00:04:30.543 --> 00:04:32.427
Who holds my contract?!

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:45.938
Your mother.

00:04:47.843 --> 00:04:50.928
Yeah, she, uh, showed it to me
right before I bent her over.

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:57.187
I want a name.

00:04:57.711 --> 00:04:59.317
- Or else...
- Or what?

00:05:00.641 --> 00:05:03.446
You're gonna squirt
your holy water in both ends?

00:05:03.942 --> 00:05:05.456
Please.

00:05:05.540 --> 00:05:08.246
Brother, that's like a fleabite
compared to what's coming to me

00:05:08.293 --> 00:05:09.966
if I tell you jack.

00:05:12.641 --> 00:05:14.007
Do what you want.

00:05:14.043 --> 00:05:18.137
The only thing I'm scared
is the demon holding your ticket.

00:05:32.661 --> 00:05:34.326
How does that feel?
Does that feel good?

00:05:36.641 --> 00:05:37.935
Go ahead.

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:41.087
Send me back to hell...

00:05:42.144 --> 00:05:44.318
'Cause when you get there,
I'll be waiting for you...

00:05:45.243 --> 00:05:46.769
With a few pals who are dying

00:05:46.771 --> 00:05:49.697
for a nice little meet and greet
Dean Winchester.

00:05:52.141 --> 00:05:53.276
Should I?

00:05:53.943 --> 00:05:56.526
Send him someplace
he can't hurt anyone else.

00:06:09.743 --> 00:06:11.488
You ran the prints twice?

00:06:11.540 --> 00:06:12.776
Are you sure?

00:06:14.741 --> 00:06:17.906
Okay. Yeah,
just chalk it up to lab error.

00:06:19.043 --> 00:06:20.637
Don't I know it. Okay.

00:06:20.741 --> 00:06:22.656
Thanks.
Yeah, I'll tell the lieutenant.

00:06:23.242 --> 00:06:24.437
Bury the body?

00:06:24.741 --> 00:06:26.265
Yeah.

00:06:26.533 --> 00:06:29.127
Looks like these demons
ride 'em hard just for kicks.

00:06:33.043 --> 00:06:34.488
What was the phone call about?

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:36.298
Remember that thing in the paper yesterday?

00:06:36.342 --> 00:06:38.637
"Stripper suffocates dude with thighs"?

00:06:38.682 --> 00:06:39.807
The other thing.

00:06:39.841 --> 00:06:41.798
Right,
the guy that walks into the E.R.

00:06:41.832 --> 00:06:43.687
and kneels over dead.
His stomach's ripped out?

00:06:43.810 --> 00:06:45.798
His liver, actually.
Anyways, I just found out

00:06:45.822 --> 00:06:47.865
- something pretty damn interesting.
- What?

00:06:47.942 --> 00:06:51.108
The dead body covered
in bloody fingerprints, not the victim's.

00:06:52.141 --> 00:06:54.776
Okay, great. My man Dave Caruso
will be stoked to hear it.

00:06:54.822 --> 00:06:58.925
Those fingerprints match a guy
who died in 1981.

00:06:59.740 --> 00:07:00.738
Really?

00:07:01.721 --> 00:07:03.437
So, what are we talking?

00:07:03.483 --> 00:07:05.668
Uh, walking dead? Walking, killing dead?

00:07:05.743 --> 00:07:06.815
Maybe.

00:07:07.241 --> 00:07:09.747
Zombies do like the other other white meat.

00:07:13.041 --> 00:07:14.935
Speaking of,
what do you care about zombies?

00:07:15.041 --> 00:07:15.925
What do you mean?

00:07:15.954 --> 00:07:17.736
Well, you've been on soul-saving detail
for months now.

00:07:17.781 --> 00:07:19.676
And we're three weeks out,
and all of a sudden,

00:07:19.723 --> 00:07:21.415
you're interested
in some hot zombie action?

00:07:21.442 --> 00:07:23.618
Hey, man, you're the one
who's been all gung ho to hunt.

00:07:23.651 --> 00:07:25.748
- I just thought I'd be doing you a favor.
- Hey, no, no, no, no, no.

00:07:25.841 --> 00:07:28.586
I didn't say I didn't want to do it, okay.
I mean obviously

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:32.326
- I want to hunt some zombies.
- Okay, fine, whatever.

00:07:38.543 --> 00:07:41.247
Yeah, the rest of the body was intact.

00:07:41.281 --> 00:07:43.408
The liver was the only organ missing.

00:07:43.942 --> 00:07:45.415
Now, where the liver was ripped out,

00:07:45.462 --> 00:07:47.945
did you happen to notice any teeth marks?

00:07:48.841 --> 00:07:50.476
Can I see your badges?

00:07:50.540 --> 00:07:51.788
Of course, sure.

00:07:55.740 --> 00:07:59.045
- Fine. So you're cops and morons.
- Excuse me?

00:07:59.081 --> 00:08:02.396
- No, no. We're very smart.
- The liver was not ripped out.

00:08:09.442 --> 00:08:11.135
It was removed.

00:08:11.144 --> 00:08:12.937
Surgically.

00:08:13.043 --> 00:08:15.536
By someone who knew
their way around a scalpel.

00:08:17.741 --> 00:08:19.676
Didn't you read my report?

00:08:20.231 --> 00:08:22.728
Of course we did. Oh, it was riveting.

00:08:22.740 --> 00:08:25.067
It was a real page-turner, just delightful.

00:08:26.241 --> 00:08:27.827
- You done?
- I think so.

00:08:27.853 --> 00:08:29.447
Please go away.

00:08:29.491 --> 00:08:30.676
Sure.

00:08:36.243 --> 00:08:37.307
What?

00:08:37.911 --> 00:08:38.786
Nothing.

00:08:38.842 --> 00:08:41.126
So, that kind of punches a hole
in our zombie theory, huh,

00:08:41.163 --> 00:08:42.197
that scalpel thing?

00:08:42.241 --> 00:08:45.195
Yeah, zombie with skills,
"Dr. Quinn, medicine zombie".

00:08:46.041 --> 00:08:47.317
Maybe we're on the wrong track, Dean,

00:08:47.351 --> 00:08:48.866
looking for hacked-up corpses.

00:08:48.942 --> 00:08:50.568
What should we be looking for?

00:08:50.644 --> 00:08:52.037
Survivors.

00:08:52.070 --> 00:08:54.379
This isn't zombie lunch.
This is organ theft.

00:08:55.643 --> 00:08:58.098
I told the cops all of this yesterday.

00:08:58.140 --> 00:08:59.838
I don't want to talk about it anymore.

00:08:59.882 --> 00:09:01.586
It's just a couple of questions, sir.

00:09:01.633 --> 00:09:02.828
Hey, man.

00:09:03.242 --> 00:09:05.416
I just got my kidney stolen.

00:09:06.241 --> 00:09:07.558
I'm tired.

00:09:07.642 --> 00:09:10.005
We'll be out of here quick.
Don't you want to get the guy?

00:09:10.041 --> 00:09:12.086
Will it get me back my kidney?

00:09:13.642 --> 00:09:15.668
So what's the last thing you remember?

00:09:15.741 --> 00:09:17.197
Feeding my meter.

00:09:18.793 --> 00:09:20.576
He jumped from behind...

00:09:20.613 --> 00:09:23.826
and then I wake up strapped to a table.

00:09:23.842 --> 00:09:29.087
And then the worst pain
you could possibly imagine, only worse.

00:09:29.742 --> 00:09:32.706
And then I black out again.
Thank god.

00:09:32.742 --> 00:09:34.966
And then I wake up screaming

00:09:35.041 --> 00:09:37.259
in some no-tell motel

00:09:37.291 --> 00:09:39.937
in a bathtub full of ice.

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:41.938
Do you remember anything
about the surgery know,

00:09:41.962 --> 00:09:44.768
what the guy looked like,
any details about the room?

00:09:45.542 --> 00:09:47.207
Let me think about that.

00:09:47.244 --> 00:09:48.557
Yeah...

00:09:49.241 --> 00:09:52.758
One thing is coming back to me.
You know what I remember?

00:09:52.843 --> 00:09:55.308
Getting my kidney cut out of my body!

00:10:01.841 --> 00:10:03.817
- So, I got a theory.
- Yeah?

00:10:03.842 --> 00:10:05.577
Yeah, I talked to Mr. Giggle's doctor.

00:10:05.614 --> 00:10:08.067
Turns out his incisions
were sewn up with silk.

00:10:08.342 --> 00:10:10.398
- That's weird.
- Yeah, nowadays it is,

00:10:10.442 --> 00:10:12.497
but silk used to be the suture of choice

00:10:12.530 --> 00:10:15.336
back in the early 19th century.
It was really problematic.

00:10:15.374 --> 00:10:17.086
Patients would get massive infections.

00:10:17.141 --> 00:10:19.158
The death rate was insane.

00:10:19.240 --> 00:10:20.388
- Good times.
- Right,

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:22.326
so doctors,
they had to do whatever they could

00:10:22.364 --> 00:10:23.836
to keep infections from spreading.

00:10:23.938 --> 00:10:26.179
- One way was maggots.
- Dude, I'm eating.

00:10:26.221 --> 00:10:28.639
It actually kind of worked
because maggots, they eat bad tissue,

00:10:28.665 --> 00:10:31.471
and they leave good tissue.
And get this. When they found our guy,

00:10:31.504 --> 00:10:35.048
- his body cavity was stuffed full of maggots.
- Dude, I'm eating.

00:10:35.081 --> 00:10:36.649
Alright let me get this straight.

00:10:37.741 --> 00:10:39.737
- So, people are getting ganked, right?
- Yeah.

00:10:39.783 --> 00:10:42.408
A little "antiques roadshow" surgery,
some organ theft.

00:10:42.453 --> 00:10:44.869
- But why does that sound familiar?
- Because you heard it before.

00:10:44.942 --> 00:10:47.545
When you we a kid... from dad.

00:10:49.744 --> 00:10:51.256
Doc Benton...

00:10:51.264 --> 00:10:53.568
real-life doctor, lived in New Hampshire,

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:55.778
brilliant and obsessed with alchemy,

00:10:55.841 --> 00:10:58.437
especially how to live forever.

00:10:58.542 --> 00:11:01.226
So, in 1816,
doc abandons his practice and...

00:11:01.241 --> 00:11:03.596
Right, yeah, nobody hears from him
for like 20 years,

00:11:03.641 --> 00:11:05.218
and all of sudden,
people start showing up dead.

00:11:05.303 --> 00:11:08.625
Dead or missing an organ
or the hand or some other kind of part.

00:11:08.644 --> 00:11:10.605
'Cause whatever he was doing
was actually working.

00:11:10.641 --> 00:11:13.427
He just kept on ticking.
Parts would wear out, he'd replace them.

00:11:13.441 --> 00:11:15.655
But I thought dad hunted him down
and took his heart out.

00:11:15.740 --> 00:11:18.567
Yeah, I guess doc
must have plugged in a new one.

00:11:20.042 --> 00:11:21.697
All right, where's he doing the deed?

00:11:21.741 --> 00:11:24.535
According to this, Ben's picky
about where he sets up his lab.

00:11:24.644 --> 00:11:27.827
He likes dense forest
with access to a river or stream

00:11:27.841 --> 00:11:29.446
- or some kind of freshwater.
- Why?

00:11:29.543 --> 00:11:32.918
Because that's where he likes
to dump the bile

00:11:32.963 --> 00:11:35.707
and intestines and fecal matter.

00:11:36.741 --> 00:11:38.177
Lost your appetite yet?

00:11:41.783 --> 00:11:43.749
Maybe I can stay mad at you.

00:13:16.652 --> 00:13:18.505
No please.

00:13:20.372 --> 00:13:21.628
No.

00:13:31.192 --> 00:13:33.727
No, no.

00:13:56.803 --> 00:13:58.778
So these are all the cabins.

00:13:58.862 --> 00:14:00.526
They most have been abandonned
for years.

00:14:00.562 --> 00:14:02.026
So what the hell
are we waiting for?

00:14:12.202 --> 00:14:14.225
They got finally got a bate on Bella.

00:14:14.273 --> 00:14:15.457
I'm listenning.

00:14:15.462 --> 00:14:16.889
Rufus Turner.

00:14:16.923 --> 00:14:18.609
Who's that? Like a Cleveland steamer?

00:14:18.652 --> 00:14:20.918
He's a hunter,
or he used to be.

00:14:20.961 --> 00:14:21.957
And now?

00:14:21.991 --> 00:14:24.408
Permit mostly.
Doesn't want selling on the side.

00:14:24.453 --> 00:14:25.356
Anyway.

00:14:25.413 --> 00:14:27.749
I put the word out on Bella
months ago.

00:14:27.754 --> 00:14:30.615
He just called.
Said a woman got in touch,

00:14:30.650 --> 00:14:32.136
wanted to buy some things.

00:14:32.173 --> 00:14:33.497
And he thinks it's Bella?

00:14:33.563 --> 00:14:36.086
British accent, went by the name
Mina Chandler.

00:14:36.131 --> 00:14:37.405
She's used that before.

00:14:38.092 --> 00:14:39.475
Well, it's kinda of a sloppy move

00:14:39.524 --> 00:14:41.505
in getting in contact
with one of your old friends.

00:14:41.543 --> 00:14:44.577
A friend? ???
in fifteen years.

00:14:44.614 --> 00:14:46.808
He's not the christmas card type.

00:14:46.841 --> 00:14:48.948
I doubt she knows I know him.

00:14:49.260 --> 00:14:50.966
Canaan, Vermont.

00:14:50.974 --> 00:14:53.567
- Thanks, Bobby. We're on our way.
- One other thing.

00:14:53.572 --> 00:14:55.888
Take a bottle of Johnnie Walker Blue.

00:14:55.890 --> 00:14:57.148
Okay.

00:14:58.283 --> 00:14:59.958
- Come on. We're going after Bella.
- What?

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:02.718
- Whoa, whoa, whoa. Hold on a second.
- Come on. Would you stop? The clock's ticking.

00:15:02.754 --> 00:15:05.229
Look, I think we should stay here
and finish the cakes.

00:15:05.273 --> 00:15:07.726
- You're insane?
- Dean, there's no way she still has the colt!

00:15:07.734 --> 00:15:10.389
There was months ago! She probably
sold it the second she got it.

00:15:10.644 --> 00:15:12.527
Well, then I'll kill her.
Win-win.

00:15:13.562 --> 00:15:14.708
We're going!

00:15:15.471 --> 00:15:17.019
- No.
- Why the hell not?

00:15:17.063 --> 00:15:19.307
Dean, this is here. Now.

00:15:19.352 --> 00:15:21.139
This is what's gonna save you.

00:15:21.182 --> 00:15:23.038
What? Chasing some Frankenstein?

00:15:23.043 --> 00:15:24.658
Chasing immortality.

00:15:27.183 --> 00:15:28.807
Look, Benton can't die.

00:15:28.841 --> 00:15:31.086
We find out how he did,
we can do it to you.

00:15:31.131 --> 00:15:33.648
- What are you talking about?
- You have to die before you go to hell, right?

00:15:33.741 --> 00:15:36.586
- So, if you can never die, then...
- Wait, wait, wait. What are you saying?

00:15:39.264 --> 00:15:41.616
Did you know that this was ???
from the jump?

00:15:42.484 --> 00:15:43.668
No.

00:15:45.591 --> 00:15:48.076
- Look, I was hoping.
- So the whole zombie thing,

00:15:48.093 --> 00:15:49.486
- it was lying to me?
- I don't wanna say anything

00:15:49.494 --> 00:15:51.067
until we're sure, Dean.
All I'm trying to do

00:15:51.114 --> 00:15:52.236
is find an answer here.

00:15:52.273 --> 00:15:54.177
No. What you're trying to do is chase

00:15:54.212 --> 00:15:56.908
slicy here.
And to kill him?

00:15:56.913 --> 00:15:59.596
No. You wanna buy him
a freaking beer. You wanna study him.

00:15:59.630 --> 00:16:01.436
- I was just trying to help.
- You're not helping!

00:16:01.451 --> 00:16:03.518
You forget that if I ???
on this deal,

00:16:03.520 --> 00:16:04.708
you die.

00:16:04.711 --> 00:16:06.347
Guess what?
Living forever is well...

00:16:06.351 --> 00:16:08.636
Fine! Then, whatever the magic pill is,
I'll take it too!

00:16:08.640 --> 00:16:11.817
Oh, what is it? Sid and Nancy?
No. It's just like Bobby was saying.

00:16:11.823 --> 00:16:13.436
We kill the demon who owns the contract,

00:16:13.443 --> 00:16:16.005
and this whole damn thing gets clean.
That's our best shot.

00:16:16.021 --> 00:16:17.966
Even if you had the colt, Dean,
who you're gonna shoot?

00:16:17.974 --> 00:16:19.586
We've no idea
who holds the ticket.

00:16:19.591 --> 00:16:21.956
I'll shoot the whole hellhouse
before they slash me up.

00:16:21.971 --> 00:16:24.165
- Now, you're coming or not?
- I'm staying here.

00:16:25.923 --> 00:16:27.206
No, you're not.

00:16:27.211 --> 00:16:29.717
'Cause I'm not gonna let you
wander out in the woods alone

00:16:29.721 --> 00:16:32.198
to track some older stealing freak.

00:16:32.201 --> 00:16:34.167
- Look, let me...
- No, I'm not gonna let you.

00:16:34.170 --> 00:16:35.578
How are you gonna stop me?

00:16:37.441 --> 00:16:39.078
Look, man,

00:16:39.082 --> 00:16:41.206
we're trying to do the same thing here.

00:16:44.801 --> 00:16:46.105
I know.

00:16:50.932 --> 00:16:52.428
But I'm going.

00:16:53.644 --> 00:16:55.426
So if you wanna stay...

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:57.229
stay.

00:17:14.634 --> 00:17:16.078
Sammy, be careful.

00:17:20.273 --> 00:17:21.206
You too.

00:17:52.822 --> 00:17:54.215
What?

00:17:54.224 --> 00:17:56.865
Hi, uh, Rufus?

00:17:56.871 --> 00:17:58.048
Yeah, even if I am,

00:17:58.063 --> 00:18:00.356
the question is still the same.
What?

00:18:01.490 --> 00:18:04.087
Uh, I'm Dean Winchester.
I'm a friend of Bobby Singer's.

00:18:04.134 --> 00:18:05.135
So?

00:18:05.641 --> 00:18:07.139
You called him this morning.

00:18:07.244 --> 00:18:08.258
So?

00:18:10.344 --> 00:18:12.557
Uh, you told Bobby

00:18:12.644 --> 00:18:14.478
about a british chick
who made contact with you.

00:18:14.511 --> 00:18:15.835
And so?

00:18:15.942 --> 00:18:17.318
You know where she is?

00:18:17.351 --> 00:18:18.706
- Yeah.
- Great.

00:18:18.744 --> 00:18:19.786
Could you tell me
where I could find her?

00:18:19.842 --> 00:18:20.849
No.

00:18:20.940 --> 00:18:22.206
Course not.

00:18:22.240 --> 00:18:23.545
Look, Rufus, man...

00:18:26.141 --> 00:18:27.826
Look,
let me point something out to you.

00:18:27.842 --> 00:18:30.567
You are knocking at my door,
so don't "Look, man" me.

00:18:30.612 --> 00:18:31.746
I'm not your man.

00:18:32.744 --> 00:18:34.248
I'm sorry, sir.

00:18:35.143 --> 00:18:36.706
All right, let me tell you a little story.

00:18:36.753 --> 00:18:38.146
See, once upon a time, Bobby called me,

00:18:38.244 --> 00:18:40.746
asked me to call him
if I got a whiff of this Bela Talbot.

00:18:40.782 --> 00:18:43.775
I got a whiff. I called. The end.

00:18:43.811 --> 00:18:45.606
Okay, yeah, if you could just
tell me where she is, I mean,

00:18:45.641 --> 00:18:47.038
that would be great.

00:18:47.641 --> 00:18:49.918
- Dean Winchester, right?
- Yeah.

00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:52.706
Dean, do I look like I'm here
to help you?

00:18:53.240 --> 00:18:54.788
I'm gonna say no.

00:18:54.833 --> 00:18:56.706
Then get the hell of my property.

00:18:56.802 --> 00:18:58.228
All right, fair enough.

00:18:58.273 --> 00:19:00.277
I got one more question for you,
though.

00:19:00.744 --> 00:19:02.436
See, I got this, uh

00:19:02.440 --> 00:19:04.938
this bottle of scotch, and... uh,

00:19:05.710 --> 00:19:07.237
is this considered good?

00:19:13.172 --> 00:19:14.586
Bottoms up.

00:19:18.081 --> 00:19:20.719
You know,
I don't even bother drinking

00:19:20.762 --> 00:19:22.358
unless it's this stuff.

00:19:23.744 --> 00:19:26.195
Nectar of the gods, I'm telling you.

00:19:26.240 --> 00:19:27.838
Hey, it's a nice change, you know.

00:19:27.891 --> 00:19:30.048
Most of my whiskey's from a plastic jug.

00:19:32.344 --> 00:19:35.967
So, Bela was here because...

00:19:36.003 --> 00:19:38.076
She wanted to buy a couple of things,

00:19:38.842 --> 00:19:41.336
which is gonna take me some time
to round up.

00:19:41.440 --> 00:19:42.885
Where is she now?

00:19:45.041 --> 00:19:46.898
Can I ask you something?

00:19:47.641 --> 00:19:48.838
Sure.

00:19:49.242 --> 00:19:51.208
You got three weeks left.

00:19:51.244 --> 00:19:52.706
Why are you wasting your time

00:19:52.742 --> 00:19:56.206
chasing after that
skinny, stuck-up english girl?

00:19:59.643 --> 00:20:01.088
How do you know about that?

00:20:05.041 --> 00:20:07.277
Because I know things.

00:20:09.240 --> 00:20:12.505
I know a lot of things
about a lot of people.

00:20:13.744 --> 00:20:15.329
Is that so?

00:20:15.340 --> 00:20:18.157
I know ain't no peashooter
gonna save you.

00:20:21.240 --> 00:20:23.105
What makes you so sure?

00:20:24.344 --> 00:20:26.585
'Cause that's the job, kid.

00:20:27.242 --> 00:20:29.489
Even if you manage
to scrape out of this one,

00:20:29.583 --> 00:20:32.286
there'just gonna be something else
down the road.

00:20:33.440 --> 00:20:35.038
Folks like us...

00:20:35.742 --> 00:20:37.889
there ain't no happy ending.

00:20:39.012 --> 00:20:40.706
We all know it coming.

00:20:45.143 --> 00:20:47.346
Well, ain't you a bucket of sunshine?

00:20:52.440 --> 00:20:55.646
I'm what you've got
to look forward to if you survive.

00:20:59.242 --> 00:21:00.757
But you won't.

00:21:45.242 --> 00:21:46.605
So, Bela...

00:21:47.811 --> 00:21:49.617
Hotel Canaan.

00:21:50.141 --> 00:21:52.059
Room 39.

00:21:54.043 --> 00:21:56.016
But watch your back.

00:21:56.242 --> 00:21:57.978
I think I can handle Bela.

00:21:58.023 --> 00:22:00.295
Oh, don't be so sure about that.

00:22:00.342 --> 00:22:03.128
There are things
that you don't know about her.

00:22:03.742 --> 00:22:05.275
Oh, and you do?

00:22:05.340 --> 00:22:06.425
Right.

00:22:07.181 --> 00:22:08.777
Because you know things.

00:22:09.041 --> 00:22:09.958
Yep.

00:22:10.043 --> 00:22:12.228
And let me guess...
you lift her fingerprint?

00:22:12.244 --> 00:22:13.527
Yep.

00:22:14.153 --> 00:22:15.746
And that got you jack.

00:22:15.842 --> 00:22:17.068
Yep.

00:22:18.641 --> 00:22:20.137
She burnt them off.

00:22:21.543 --> 00:22:23.409
Probably years ago.

00:22:23.942 --> 00:22:25.719
Yeah, so you're right where we are.

00:22:25.753 --> 00:22:26.876
Nope.

00:22:31.240 --> 00:22:32.768
You do her ear?

00:22:33.643 --> 00:22:34.775
Sorry?

00:22:34.844 --> 00:22:36.699
You do her ear?

00:22:39.742 --> 00:22:41.965
Hey, man, I'll try anything once,
but I don't know.

00:22:42.014 --> 00:22:43.528
That sounds uncomfortable.

00:22:45.242 --> 00:22:48.786
Ears are as unique to humans
as fingerprints.

00:22:49.643 --> 00:22:50.788
- No kidding.
- Of course,

00:22:50.831 --> 00:22:53.259
that don't fly in the
courts over here,

00:22:54.003 --> 00:22:57.449
but in England, they're all over it.

00:23:00.242 --> 00:23:02.097
A friend of a friend...

00:23:02.632 --> 00:23:04.005
of a friend

00:23:04.041 --> 00:23:06.887
faxed me 10 pages
of confidential files

00:23:06.943 --> 00:23:08.576
within a day.

00:23:09.322 --> 00:23:13.777
All I had to send him was
one clean shot off the security camera.

00:23:15.041 --> 00:23:16.248
Right.

00:23:17.242 --> 00:23:19.175
One clean shot of her ear.

00:23:35.423 --> 00:23:38.076
The so-called Bela Talbot.

00:26:03.291 --> 00:26:04.657
Shh! Shh! Shh!

00:26:04.711 --> 00:26:06.177
It's okay. I'm here to help you.

00:26:06.190 --> 00:26:07.759
I'm here to help you.
I'm gonna help you.

00:26:17.813 --> 00:26:21.025
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.
Okay, here we go.

00:27:22.143 --> 00:27:23.628
Ok, watch your head.

00:27:25.740 --> 00:27:26.608
Sorry.

00:27:36.291 --> 00:27:38.385
Try to get straight. Try to get straight.

00:28:24.742 --> 00:28:26.619
- Where's the colt?
- Dean.

00:28:26.650 --> 00:28:28.318
No extra words.

00:28:28.742 --> 00:28:32.067
It's long gone,
across the world by now.

00:28:33.543 --> 00:28:34.626
You're lying.

00:28:34.692 --> 00:28:36.697
I'll call the buyer. Speak farsi?

00:28:38.242 --> 00:28:39.476
What the hell...

00:28:39.530 --> 00:28:41.197
Don't flatter yourself.

00:28:43.744 --> 00:28:46.306
- Don't move.
- I told you I don't have it.

00:28:46.342 --> 00:28:48.788
Oh, yeah, I'm definitely
gonna take your word for it.

00:28:58.240 --> 00:28:59.679
Don't move.

00:29:10.824 --> 00:29:11.876
It's gone.

00:29:13.242 --> 00:29:15.119
Get on a plane if you must.

00:29:18.240 --> 00:29:20.987
Track down the buyer.
You might catch up to him eventually.

00:29:26.742 --> 00:29:28.208
Are you going to kill me?

00:29:28.242 --> 00:29:29.806
Oh, yeah.

00:29:31.143 --> 00:29:32.869
You're not the cold-blooded type.

00:29:32.942 --> 00:29:34.336
You mean like you?

00:29:34.340 --> 00:29:36.028
That's true.

00:29:36.043 --> 00:29:38.945
See, I couldn't imagine
killing my parents.

00:29:40.744 --> 00:29:42.815
- I don't know what you're talking...
- Yes, you do.

00:29:44.240 --> 00:29:46.219
You were, what, 14?

00:29:46.740 --> 00:29:49.128
Folks died in some shady car accident.

00:29:49.170 --> 00:29:51.016
Police suspected a slashed brake line,

00:29:51.041 --> 00:29:53.507
but it was all too crispy to tell.

00:29:53.543 --> 00:29:55.275
Cut to little Bela...

00:29:55.320 --> 00:29:57.668
Oh, I'm sorry, Abby...

00:29:57.742 --> 00:29:59.706
inheriting millions.

00:30:00.242 --> 00:30:02.309
- How did you ev...
- Doesn't matter.

00:30:27.661 --> 00:30:29.347
They were lovely people.

00:30:30.043 --> 00:30:31.737
And I killed them.

00:30:33.242 --> 00:30:34.668
And I got rich.

00:30:34.701 --> 00:30:37.168
I can't be bothered to give a damn.

00:30:39.043 --> 00:30:41.626
Just like I don't care
what happens to you.

00:30:49.740 --> 00:30:51.617
You make me sick.

00:30:53.641 --> 00:30:55.398
Likewise.

00:31:20.742 --> 00:31:22.318
You're not worth it.

00:31:52.244 --> 00:31:53.597
It worked.

00:31:54.043 --> 00:31:55.407
He found me.

00:31:56.742 --> 00:31:58.568
No, Sam wasn't with him.

00:31:59.744 --> 00:32:01.148
But I know where they are.

00:32:07.242 --> 00:32:08.936
- Dean?
- Yeah.

00:32:09.043 --> 00:32:11.157
- Did you get the colt?
- What do you think?

00:32:11.190 --> 00:32:12.657
So, does that mean Bela is...

00:32:12.690 --> 00:32:15.239
No, no, she deserves to die
a dozen times over,

00:32:15.273 --> 00:32:16.456
but I couldn't do it.

00:32:16.543 --> 00:32:18.056
I'm really screwed, Sammy.

00:32:18.101 --> 00:32:19.766
- No, you're just...
- But you were right.

00:32:19.802 --> 00:32:21.626
Bela was a goose chase.

00:32:23.041 --> 00:32:24.326
The colt's gone,

00:32:24.331 --> 00:32:26.898
and this time I'm really screwed, Sam.

00:32:26.942 --> 00:32:28.155
Maybe not.

00:32:28.740 --> 00:32:30.719
Look, I found Benton's cabin.

00:32:30.744 --> 00:32:32.699
- You okay? Was he there?
- Yeah.

00:32:32.742 --> 00:32:33.949
- Did you kill him?
- No.

00:32:33.992 --> 00:32:36.108
- What do you mean, "no"?
- Dean, please just listen for a second.

00:32:36.141 --> 00:32:38.836
I found his lab book,
and it has the formula.

00:32:38.882 --> 00:32:41.108
- What, the live-forever formula?</i
- Yeah.

00:32:41.181 --> 00:32:42.188
Great, let me guess.

00:32:42.231 --> 00:32:43.826
I got to drink blood
out of a baby's skull?

00:32:43.842 --> 00:32:47.016
No, that's the thing.
It's not black magic.

00:32:47.043 --> 00:32:49.576
There's no blood sacrifice or anything.

00:32:50.641 --> 00:32:52.347
It's just science, Dean.

00:32:52.442 --> 00:32:55.596
Very, very extremely weird science, but...

00:32:55.641 --> 00:32:57.347
Wait, wait, wait. What are...
What are you saying? You think...

00:32:57.391 --> 00:32:59.108
Dean, I think it might be doable.

00:32:59.163 --> 00:33:00.695
I mean,
I know we've hit a lot of walls, but I...

00:33:00.744 --> 00:33:03.347
I think this formula,
I think it might be it.

00:33:03.713 --> 00:33:05.105
This could save you.

00:33:05.623 --> 00:33:07.179
Okay, so, this formula...

00:33:07.242 --> 00:33:09.387
Well, I mean, look, look,
we're not in the clear yet.

00:33:09.440 --> 00:33:10.927
There are still things that I don't get.

00:33:12.740 --> 00:33:13.557
Sam?

00:33:17.740 --> 00:33:19.039
Sammy!

00:33:29.773 --> 00:33:31.925
You can relax.

00:33:32.242 --> 00:33:34.476
It's all gonna be okay.

00:33:34.541 --> 00:33:36.318
Ain't nothing gonna happen here

00:33:36.342 --> 00:33:38.585
that you got to worry about, Sammy.

00:33:38.664 --> 00:33:42.536
Your chances of coming out
of this procedure alive?

00:33:42.641 --> 00:33:44.777
Very, very high.

00:33:44.882 --> 00:33:46.456
How do you know my name?

00:33:47.641 --> 00:33:48.706
Oh...

00:33:50.742 --> 00:33:52.108
I know.

00:33:54.043 --> 00:33:57.257
You think I'm some kind of monster,
don't you?

00:33:57.443 --> 00:34:01.496
Well, I got to tell you,
I have never done one thing

00:34:01.543 --> 00:34:03.956
that I did not have to do.

00:34:04.001 --> 00:34:09.126
This whole eternal-life thing
is very high-maintenance.

00:34:10.782 --> 00:34:14.556
If something goes bad,
like my eyes here...

00:34:15.643 --> 00:34:17.815
you got to replace them.

00:34:22.641 --> 00:34:24.646
And sometimes things get damaged,

00:34:24.690 --> 00:34:29.449
like when your father cut out my heart.
Now, that...

00:34:29.543 --> 00:34:33.385
That was very inconvenient.

00:34:36.041 --> 00:34:39.226
So,
I'm sure that you can understand

00:34:39.242 --> 00:34:42.067
all the joy I felt

00:34:42.101 --> 00:34:46.788
when I read all
about myself here in his journal.

00:34:52.791 --> 00:34:55.175
Kind of makes this whole thing

00:34:56.244 --> 00:35:01.306
just feel like some
kind of family reunion, don't it?

00:35:02.641 --> 00:35:05.367
Well, I guess it's about time

00:35:05.740 --> 00:35:08.556
that we get this thing started.

00:35:25.141 --> 00:35:27.498
Shoot all you want.

00:35:47.143 --> 00:35:48.717
A knife?

00:35:51.242 --> 00:35:56.688
What part of immortality
do you not understand?

00:35:59.740 --> 00:36:02.666
Pity about the heart, though.

00:36:02.842 --> 00:36:06.056
It was a brand-new one.

00:36:06.143 --> 00:36:07.416
Good.

00:36:07.821 --> 00:36:10.116
It should be pumping nice and strong...

00:36:11.243 --> 00:36:15.278
Sending this stuff throughout
your whole body.

00:36:16.241 --> 00:36:17.717
See, I picked up your little

00:36:17.762 --> 00:36:20.315
bottle upstairs and dipped the knife in it.

00:36:34.713 --> 00:36:36.817
Oh, hiya, doc.

00:36:37.742 --> 00:36:39.996
Wakey, wakey, eggs and bac-y.

00:36:42.040 --> 00:36:44.105
- Please.
- Please what?

00:36:44.121 --> 00:36:46.268
You've been killing poor bastards
for over 150 years

00:36:46.310 --> 00:36:48.138
and now you got a request?
Shut up.

00:36:48.173 --> 00:36:50.905
No, you don't understand.
I can help you. I know

00:36:50.943 --> 00:36:52.125
what you need.

00:36:52.163 --> 00:36:53.826
We might have to cut him up
into little bits. You know,

00:36:53.862 --> 00:36:55.748
this immortality thing is a bitch.

00:36:55.783 --> 00:36:59.077
I can read the formula for you.

00:36:59.743 --> 00:37:03.027
The whole immortality...

00:37:03.041 --> 00:37:06.926
Forever young, never die.

00:37:25.252 --> 00:37:26.368
What?

00:37:29.243 --> 00:37:30.835
I mean,
we're talking hell in three weeks.

00:37:30.873 --> 00:37:33.067
Or needing a new pancreas
in like half a century.

00:37:33.071 --> 00:37:34.846
Yeah, well, you can't exactly get those
at a kwik-e-mart.

00:37:34.884 --> 00:37:37.467
It's not perfect, but it buys us more time
to think of something better.

00:37:37.540 --> 00:37:39.896
We just need time, Dean.
I mean, please, just...

00:37:40.400 --> 00:37:42.016
just think about it.

00:37:45.641 --> 00:37:46.728
No.

00:37:47.242 --> 00:37:49.547
- Dean, don't you want to live?
- What he is isn't living.

00:37:49.590 --> 00:37:50.955
- Look, this is simple.
- Simple?

00:37:50.993 --> 00:37:54.215
To me it is, okay.
Black or white; human, not human.

00:37:55.742 --> 00:37:57.396
See, what the doc is

00:37:57.403 --> 00:37:59.297
is a freakin' monster.

00:37:59.342 --> 00:38:00.826
I can't do it.

00:38:01.342 --> 00:38:03.176
I would rather go to hell.

00:38:03.721 --> 00:38:07.076
You don't understand.
I can help you!

00:38:10.473 --> 00:38:12.277
Now, I'm gonna take care of him.

00:38:12.741 --> 00:38:14.806
You can help me or not.
It's up to you.

00:38:45.753 --> 00:38:47.106
No! No!

00:38:47.181 --> 00:38:48.929
Don't! Stop it!

00:38:48.973 --> 00:38:51.436
I can help you! No!

00:38:51.482 --> 00:38:53.295
Enjoy forever in there, doc.

00:38:55.121 --> 00:38:56.509
Let me out!

00:39:01.210 --> 00:39:03.699
I can save you!

00:39:03.740 --> 00:39:05.608
No. Don't.

00:40:19.134 --> 00:40:20.306
Hiya, Bela.

00:40:20.350 --> 00:40:22.446
Here's a fun fact you may not know...

00:40:22.481 --> 00:40:24.219
I felt your hand in my pocket

00:40:24.233 --> 00:40:25.888
when you swiped that motel receipt.

00:40:25.922 --> 00:40:26.895
You don't understand.

00:40:26.942 --> 00:40:29.286
Oh, I'm pretty sure
I understand perfectly.

00:40:29.344 --> 00:40:31.775
You see, I noticed something interesting
in your hotel room,

00:40:31.840 --> 00:40:35.135
something tucked above the door.
An herb...

00:40:35.182 --> 00:40:36.935
devil's shoestring.

00:40:37.440 --> 00:40:39.465
Well, there's only one use for that...

00:40:39.840 --> 00:40:41.878
holding hellhounds at bay.

00:40:42.242 --> 00:40:43.335
So, you know what I did?
I went back,

00:40:43.342 --> 00:40:45.288
and I took another look at
your folks' obit.

00:40:45.333 --> 00:40:48.086
Turns out they died 10 years ago today.

00:40:48.740 --> 00:40:50.255
You didn't kill them.

00:40:50.601 --> 00:40:52.658
A demon did your dirty work.

00:40:52.692 --> 00:40:55.538
You made a deal, didn't you, Bela?

00:40:55.693 --> 00:40:57.516
And it's come due.

00:41:03.763 --> 00:41:05.615
I can take care of them for you.

00:41:08.141 --> 00:41:10.067
And it won't even cost you anything.

00:41:12.243 --> 00:41:15.717
For 10 whole years.

00:41:21.242 --> 00:41:23.896
Is that why you stole the colt, huh?

00:41:24.243 --> 00:41:25.795
To try to wiggle out of your deal?

00:41:25.840 --> 00:41:28.416
- Our gun for your soul?
- Yes.

00:41:28.453 --> 00:41:30.806
But stealing the colt
wasn't quite enough, I'm guessing.

00:41:30.893 --> 00:41:32.567
They changed the deal.

00:41:33.743 --> 00:41:35.507
They wanted me to kill Sam.

00:41:35.542 --> 00:41:37.277
Really? Wow.

00:41:37.342 --> 00:41:38.998
Demons untrustworthy...

00:41:39.242 --> 00:41:40.438
Shocker.

00:41:41.141 --> 00:41:43.047
That's kind of a tight deadline, too.

00:41:43.123 --> 00:41:44.576
What time is it?

00:41:44.641 --> 00:41:47.876
Oh, look at that. Almost midnight.

00:41:48.240 --> 00:41:50.177
Dean, listen, I need help.

00:41:50.241 --> 00:41:52.179
Sweetheart, we are weeks past help.

00:41:52.223 --> 00:41:53.827
I know I don't deserve it.

00:41:53.862 --> 00:41:54.905
You know what? You're right.
You don't.

00:41:54.942 --> 00:41:56.695
But you know
what the bitch of the bunch is?

00:41:56.741 --> 00:41:59.806
If you would have just come to us sooner
and asked for help,

00:41:59.842 --> 00:42:02.056
we probably could have taken the colt
and saved you.

00:42:02.342 --> 00:42:04.558
I know, and saved yourself.

00:42:05.243 --> 00:42:07.135
I know about your deal, Dean.

00:42:07.221 --> 00:42:08.507
Wnd who told you that?

00:42:08.543 --> 00:42:10.208
The demon that holds it.

00:42:10.240 --> 00:42:11.748
She holds mine, too.

00:42:12.241 --> 00:42:14.757
- She says she holds every deal.
- She?

00:42:14.842 --> 00:42:16.016
Her name's Lilith.

00:42:16.741 --> 00:42:17.876
Lilith?

00:42:19.742 --> 00:42:21.156
Why should I believe you?

00:42:21.971 --> 00:42:24.185
You shouldn't, but it's the truth.

00:42:24.222 --> 00:42:25.775
This can't help you, Bela.

00:42:26.251 --> 00:42:28.297
Not now.
Why are you telling me this?

00:42:28.741 --> 00:42:31.657
Because just maybe you can kill the bitch.

00:42:35.743 --> 00:42:37.496
I'll see you in hell.



00:00:0.500 --> 00:00:2.00
